# Line endings, so a clone is runnable on the platform it lands on:
#  - cmd.exe is fussy about LF batch files
#  - bash refuses a "#!/bin/sh\r" shebang
# Without this, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true gets a CRLF
# build_linux.sh, and a Linux clone with autocrlf=input can get an LF
# build_windows.cmd.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
CMakeCache.txt text eol=lf
